<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<project baseDir="..\bin\Release" outputDir="..\bin\Release\Obfuscated" xmlns="http://confuser.codeplex.com">
  <!--
    ConfuserEx project for Core.Licensing (Licensing-Plan.md, Phase 6).

    Scoped to Core.Licensing.dll ONLY, per the plan's own guidance: this
    is the assembly worth raising the bar on (fingerprinting, signing,
    validation), and NOT PosSystem.App.exe itself — obfuscating a WPF exe
    risks breaking x:Class/XAML type resolution, InitializeComponent, and
    resource lookups in ways that can't be verified without a real WPF
    runtime to click through, which isn't available in the environment
    this was written in. If PosSystem.App.exe obfuscation is wanted later,
    it needs its own carefully-scoped rule set (excluding anything XAML
    touches) and real testing on a Windows machine, not a blind expansion
    of this file.

    "normal" preset covers renaming, control-flow obfuscation, and
    anti-tamper — a reasonable default without needing per-protection
    tuning for a first pass. Revisit if ConfuserEx's own docs recommend
    against something here once actually run (e.g. anti-tamper is known
    to sometimes conflict with certain AV heuristics — false positives
    are a real risk worth watching for on client machines, not just a
    theoretical one).
  -->
  <rule pattern="true" preset="normal" inherit="false" />
  <module path="Core.Licensing.dll" />
</project>
